<section class="placeholder-text container">
  <p>
    As the Brown community looks toward April to bring in spring after a long winter, everyone readies themselves for the long-awaited housing lottery. Responsible for determining where each student will be living for the upcoming school year, the housing process at Brown is one of great anticipation as well as confusion, especially for rising sophomores who have never gone through the process before.
  </p>
  <p>
    For this reason, The Herald decided to investigate housing trends to give readers more information on how last year’s lottery worked, and real-time updates of available dorms as students select them during the 3-day selection process. 
  </p>
  <p>
    This information has been synthesized into a map of campus with each residence hall color-coded based on percentage availability. Students can filter this information based on their preferences, such as by room type and gender, and can control a slider that shows room availability over time.
  </p>
</section>

